# Cloudflare Pages redirects
# Order matters: explicit rules first, then wildcards.
#
# Status codes:
#   200 = rewrite (serve target's content with request's URL — address bar stays)
#   301 = permanent redirect (browser follows, address bar updates to target)
#
# Short aliases use 200 so /tip shows the page with /tip in the address bar.
# Old .html URLs use 301 so visitors and search engines see the clean URL.

# === Special: index.html (must come before wildcard to avoid /index) ===
/index.html           /                   301
/tools/index.html     /tools              301
/blog/index.html      /blog               301

# === /api — redirect to api.toolsbase.net/docs (content served by Worker) ===
/api/  https://api.toolsbase.net/docs  301
/api   https://api.toolsbase.net/docs  301

